==Summer Sweep Up Slayer & More==
Summer Sweep Up is here, bringing a wave of skilling and Slayer updates - let’s delve into everything we’ve been tinkering with!

===Blocklists: Your Tasks, Your Rules===
Ever wanted to tell a Slayer master, "Not today, sir!"? Well, now you can! Each Slayer master now has their own individual block list, putting the power in your hands to avoid those pesky, annoying tasks when you're just not feeling it.

[[File:Summer Sweep Up Slayer & More (1).png|thumb|500px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2025/newsposts/2025-07-17/BlockInterface.png here]!'']]

* Blocking a task from one Slayer master stops that master from giving it to you again - but other masters are still fair game.
* Attempting to block a task that the Slayer master doesn’t assign will get you a polite little warning, instead of wasted points.
* All your previously blocked tasks? Points are refunded automatically when you log in.
* Sharing is caring, but only for Turael, Aya, and Spria. Everyone else gets their own unique lists and block prices:    
** Turael/Aya and Spria: 40 points
** Mazchna/Achtryn: 50 points
** Vannaka: 60 points
** Chaeldar: 70 points
** Konar: 80 points
** Nieve/Steve: 90 points
** Duradel/Kuradal: 100 points
** Krystilia: 100 points
* Use the "View List" option on the Slayer Rewards task tab to see the full set of creatures each Slayer Master can assign. Every Master has their own unique list, and from here you can block tasks at the costs listed above.
* Green tick - tasks available to block.
* Red circle - tasks you’ve already blocked.
* Yellow padlock - tasks this Slayer Master cannot assign.
* Green padlock - your current task (you therefore cannot get it as a new task, but it's still available to block).

[[File:Summer Sweep Up Slayer & More (2).png|thumb|500px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2025/newsposts/2025-07-17/SlayerList.png here]!'']]

===Alloyed Adventures with Metal Dragons===
Dragon Slayer grind, streamlined! Bronze, Iron, Steel, Mithril, Adamant, and Runite dragons have been unified under a single "Metal Dragons" task.

* One task to rule them all! Any metal dragon you kill counts toward this task, making it simpler and more flexible.
* Tasks now start low (between 30-50 dragons) but can be extended all the way up to 150-200.
* Any existing unlocks or extensions for old metal dragons are refunded on login, and your current task will automatically convert to the new Metal Dragons task.

Simpler, flexible, and still plenty of dragons to slay. Now go forth and smite those metallic foes!

===Slayer Unlocks Get a Point Makeover===
Ever feel like your Slayer points were vanishing faster than your HP at a Vardorvis rampage? We’ve gone through all the Slayer unlocks and given them a little love. Some of the more basic unlocks were costing way more points than they were worth, so we’ve rebalanced them to make your points go further. 

* Slug Salter - reduced from 80 points → 10 points
* Reptile Freezer - reduced from 90 points → 10 points
* Ring Bling - reduced from 300 points → 150 points
* Bigger and Badder - reduced from 150 points → 50 points

If you’ve already unlocked any of these, don’t worry! You’ll get the appropriate points refunded automatically when you log in, with a nice little message telling you exactly how many points you’ve got back.

===Lunar Key Drop Rates Updated===
We’ve adjusted the drop rates for Lunar Keys from various PVM encounters in the Twilight Temple dungeon to make obtaining them feel fairer across different combat levels.

* Frost Nagua: 1/1052
* Ice Giant: 1/2190
* Ice Spider: 1/2036
* Chilled Jelly: 1/961
* Brutal Blue Dragon: 1/250
* Blue Dragon: 1/1216
* Baby Blue Dragon: 1/2290
* Ice Warrior: 1/2112
* Icefiend: 1/3058
* Frost Crab: 1/3011
* Cave Crawler: 1/2260
* Amoxliatl: 1/150
* The Hueycoatl: 1/75

We hope these changes improve the lower-end combat scaling, while keeping high-levels challenging and rewarding.

===Miscellaneous & Slayer Updates===

* Lowered the cost of the Task Storage from slayer rewards from 1000 points → 500. For purchases made previously, 500 points will be refunded upon login.
* You can now use Slayer Task Storage for Wilderness Slayer tasks
* The Granite hammer now has a 30% Golembane effect, dealing 30% extra damage and accuracy against all golem-type creatures. This includes Gargoyles and covers all phases of the Grotesque Guardians.
* Selected Slayer creatures that previously dropped 1-2 noted herbs now drop unnoted herbs, allowing for the herb sack to be utilised more effectively.
* Helmet of the Moon has been added to the Collection Log and will retroactively unlock for all eligible accounts.
* Mark of Darkness now lasts 3 minutes by default.
* Low-level Slayer master points have been buffed! Mazchna now awards 6 points per task (up from 2) and Vannaka 8 points (up from 4).
** Milestone multipliers have also been updated to give slightly more points, without surpassing their higher-level masters; Mazchna: 10th task 30 pts, 50th 90 pts; Vannaka: 10th task 40 pts, 50th 120 pts.

==A Date with Doom - Combat Achievements Coming Soon!==
We know you’ve all been eagerly awaiting the Dooms Combat Achievements, and the wait is finally over: mark your calendars for September 3rd! Get ready to test your skills and earn your rewards.

